# The Markdown files in config/ are DATA, not prose: their exact layout is parsed.
#
# - cv_base.md is read back by docx_builder.parse_markdown_cv(), which keys off the
#   `### `/`#### ` heading levels, the `*` bullet marker, the trailing ` <br>` and the
#   `Tech:` line sitting directly under the last bullet. Prettier rewrites `*` to `-`,
#   inserts a blank line after every heading and indents the `Tech:` continuation line,
#   so a format-on-save silently changes what the generator sees.
# - The prompt files (ats_prompt.md, ats_review_prompt.md, cover_letter_prompt.md) are
#   sent to the model verbatim, placeholders and numbering included.
# - projects.md / projects_list.md are the profile the CV and the fit score are grounded
#   in; reformatting them only produces noise in the diff.
#
# Patterns are deliberately unanchored (`**/config/`, not `config/`) so they still
# match when VS Code's workspace root is a PARENT folder and this ignore file is
# resolved from there.
config/
**/config/
**/cv_base.md
**/projects.md
**/projects_list.md
**/*_prompt.md

